do I download Tonies on my Toniebox 1?\n\n# How do I set up a Toniebox 1?\n\nLet us show you how to get your Toniebox 1 up and running within minutes. Have fun!\n\nIf you have trouble installing your Toniebox, please contact our support, stating your Toniebox 1 ID.\n\n# How to set up your Toniebox 1:\n\n \n\n## Web setup\n\nUsing my.tonies.com/setup\n\n  1. ### Get started with setup\n\nNavigate to my.tonies.com/setup on your device. If you have not logged in or created a free Tonie-Account yet, you will be greeted by the page shown below. Click on 'I want to begin'.\n\nImage: deskSetup1.jpg\n \n\n  2. ### Create your account\n\nHere you can sign up for your free Tonie-Account by entering in your information and clicking 'Sign Up Now'. If you have already created a Tonie-Account, click on 'Log In Now' and login using your credentials.\n\nImage: deskSetup2.jpg\n \n\n  3. ### Gather what you need\n\nMake sure you have access to a 2.4GHz Wi-Fi connection, your Toniebox 1, and the Toniebox 1 Charging Station. Also, make sure your computer is connected via Wi-Fi and not plugged in directly through an ethernet cable. Once you are ready, click on 'I want to begin!'.\n\nImage: deskSetup3.jpg\n \n\n  4. ### Enter your Toniebox 1 ID\n\nEnter your Toniebox 1 ID. This is the 8 digit ID that can be found on the bottom of your Toniebox 1. Make sure the Toniebox 1 is not on the charger during this step or you will not be able to see the Toniebox 1 ID. Once you have entered your Toniebox 1 ID, click on 'Great, go ahead'.\n\nImage: TonieboxStep3.png\n \n\n  5. ### Name your Toniebox 1\n\nHere you can name your Toniebox 1. Once you have entered a name, click on 'Onwards!'\n\nImage: deskSetup5.jpg\n \n\n  6. ### Put your Toniebox 1 in setup mode\n\nIf you have not already, place the Toniebox 1 on the charger to turn it on. Then pinch both ears for about 5 seconds until you hear an audio chime and the LED begins to flash blue. Wait for about 20 seconds until you hear a second audio chime. Then click on 'Then get started!'.\n## Using the tonies app on an iPhone with iOS\n\nUsing the tonies app on an iPhone with iOS\n\n  1. ### Download the tonies app\n\nDownload the tonies app from the App Store (iPhone). Open the tonies app and login or create your free Tonie-Account if you have not already done so. Once you are logged in, tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Step_1.jpg\n \n\n  2. ### Tap the plus (+) sign\n\nTap the red plus (+) sign next to 'Toniebox'\nImage: Step_2.jpg\n \n\n  3. ### Tap 'Start Setup Process'\n\nTap 'Start Setup Process' at the bottom of the screen to start the setup process.\nImage: IMG_0582.PNG\n \n\n  4. ### Confirm Toniebox 1 is on\n\nBefore proceeding, ensure your Toniebox 1 is turned on and the LED is flashing green by placing it on top of the charging station that is plugged into a power source. Once done, tap 'Continue'.\nImage: IMG_0583.PNG\n \n\n  5. ### Pinch both ears\n\nNow, while the Toniebox 1 is on and plugged in, pinch and hold both ears for about 5 seconds until the LED flashes blue and you hear an audio tone. Once you hear the audio tone, tap 'Continue'. \nImage: IMG_0584.PNGImage: IMG_0607.png\n \n\n  6. ### Confirm LED color\n\nYou will then be asked to select what LED is currently shown on top of the Toniebox 1. The LED should be blinking/pulsing blue at this stage. Simply tap the 'Blue LED' button when prompted.\nImage: IMG_0652.png\n \n\n  7. ### Start setup wizard\n\nThe setup wizard will now start the setup process, and after a few seconds, you will see a 'Discovering' window at the bottom of the screen. Please wait for the setup wizard to load and locate your Toniebox 1. \nImage: IMG_0585.PNGImage: IMG_0586.PNG\n \n\n  8. ### Set up accessory\n\nOnce your Toniebox 1 has been located, you will see a 'Set Up Accessory' window at the bottom of the screen, and it will ask you to pair your Toniebox 1 with the tonies app and your smartphone. Once prompted, simply tap 'Set Up' at the bottom. \nImage: IMG_0587.PNG\n \n\n  9. ### Finish setup in app\n\nAfter the Toniebox 1 has completed pairing, you will see a 'Finish Setup in App' screen at the bottom. To finalize the setup process, tap on the 'Continue in App' button. \nImage: IMG_0588.PNG\n \n\n  10. ### Let Toniebox 1 info load\n\nWait until the 'Loading Toniebox 1 information' step is completed and has a green checkmark next to it, then tap on 'Continue'. \nImage: IMG_0589.PNGImage: IMG_0590.PNG\n \n\n  11. Now you will see a list of available Wi-Fi networks. Tap the name of your Wi-Fi network to continue.\nImage: IMG_0595.PNG\n  \n  12. ### Connect to your Wi-Fi\n\nEnter your Wi-Fi password. Tip: Tap the 'eye' icon on the right-hand side to see your password and ensure that all capitalization and spelling are correct. Once you have entered the correct password, tap 'Continue'. \nImage: IMG_0598.PNG\n \n\n  13. ### Connect and update\n\nWait while the Toniebox 1 establishes a connection with your Wi-Fi and downloads any available updates. This process may take a minute or two and you may hear multiple sounds or beeps while the Toniebox 1 connects. *If you run into an error message, take a look at our support article here: The Toniebox 1 flashes red and reports an error\nImage: IMG_0600.PNGImage: IMG_0601.PNG\n \n\n  14. ### Toniebox 1 is ready to play!\n\nOnce your Toniebox 1 is finished connecting to your Wi-Fi and downloading any necessary updates, you will hear a welcome message from the Toniebox 1 speaker and see a screen that says 'Congratulations! Your Toniebox 1 is ready to play!'. The Toniebox 1 LED should also now be solid green.\nNote: You can tap the 'Personalize now (recommended)' button to adjust specific settings such as volume and the Toniebox 1 name, however, these settings can be adjusted at any point in time.\nImage: IMG_0602.PNG\n \n\n  15. Now, your Toniebox 1 is all setup and ready for Tonies! Place a Tonie on the Toniebox 1 and it will begin downloading its content and the LED will begin blinking blue. Once your Tonie is finished downloading all of its content, the LED on the Toniebox 1 will change to solid green and an audio chime will play. Now that Tonie can play even without a Wi-Fi connection. For more information on downloading Tonies, check out our support article here: How do I download Tonies on my Toniebox 1?\n\n## Using the tonies app on an Android smartphone\n\nUsing the tonies app on an Android smartphone\n\n  1. ### Download the tonies app\n\nDownload the tonies app from the Google Play Store (Android). Open the tonies app and login or create your free Tonie-Account if you have not already done so. Once you are logged in, tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Step_1.jpg\n \n\n  2. ### Tap the plus (+) sign\n\nTap the red plus (+) sign next to 'Toniebox'\nImage: Step_2.jpg\n \n\n  3. ### Tap 'Start Setup Process'\n\nTap 'Start Setup Process' at the bottom of the screen to start the setup process.\nImage: 1.jpg\n \n\n  4. ### Enter your Toniebox 1 ID\n\nThis is the 8 digit ID that can be found on the bottom of your Toniebox 1. Make sure the Toniebox 1 is not on the charger or you will not be able to see the Toniebox 1 ID. Once you have entered your Toniebox 1 ID, tap 'Continue'.\nImage: 3.jpg\n \n\n  5. ### Confirm Toniebox 1 is on\n\nBefore proceeding, ensure your Toniebox 1 is turned on and the LED is flashing green by placing it on top of the charging station that is plugged into a power source. Once done, tap 'Continue'.\nImage: IMG_0583.PNG\n \n\n  6. ### Place the Toniebox 1 on the charger \n\nPlace the Toniebox 1 on the charger to turn it on if you have not already done so. Then pinch both ears for about 5 seconds until you hear an audio chime and the LED begins to flash blue. Wait for about 20 seconds until you hear a second audio chime. Once you hear the second audio chime and the LED is slowly pulsing blue, tap 'Continue'.\nNote: If you run into an error message, or see a red flashing LED at this stage, take a look at our support article here: The Toniebox 1 flashes red and reports an error\nImage: 5.jpg\n \n\n  7. ### Confirm LED color\n\nYou will then be asked to select what LED is currently shown on top of the Toniebox 1. The LED should be slowly pulsing blue (in and out) at this stage. Simply tap the 'Blue Pulsing LED' button when prompted. \nImage: 6.jpg\n \n\n  8. ### Connect to device\n\nNow the Toniebox 1 will attempt to connect to your smartphone. When you see the box that says 'Connect to device?', tap the 'Connect' or 'Allow' button. *If you run into an error message, take a look at our support article here: The Toniebox 1 flashes red and reports an error\nImage: 12.jpgImage: 13.jpg\n \n\n  13. ### Your Toniebox 1 is ready to play!\n\nOnce your Toniebox 1 is finished connecting to your Wi-Fi and downloading any necessary updates, you will hear a welcome message from the Toniebox 1 speaker and see a screen that says 'Congratulations! Your Toniebox 1 is ready to play!'. The Toniebox 1 LED should also now be solid green.\nNote: You can tap the 'Personalize now (recommended)' button to adjust specific settings such as volume and the Toniebox 1 name, however, these settings can be adjusted at any point in time.\nImage: IMG_0602.PNG\n \n\n  14. ### Play with your Toniebox 1!\n\nNow your Toniebox 1 is all setup and ready for Tonies! Place a Tonie on the Toniebox 1 and it will begin downloading its content and the LED will begin blinking blue. Once your Tonie is finished downloading all of its content, the LED on the Toniebox 1 will change to solid green and an audio chime will play. Now that Tonie can play even without a Wi-Fi connection. For more information on downloading Tonies, check out our support article here: How do I download Tonies on my Toniebox 1?\n\nIf you run into any issues during setup, send us a message including your Toniebox 1 ID and we will be there to help!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I edit/delete content on my special Creative-Tonie? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/10514159917586-How-do-I-edit-delete-content-on-my-special-Creative-Tonie)\nciteturn785search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; Crawled: 1.4 years ago; There are a few special Tonies that include pre-loaded content on them, but they can also function as Creative-Tonies! ... Check out our other support articles here:\n\n# How do I edit/delete content on my special Creative-Tonie?\n\nImage: Avatar\n\nRyan\n\nUpdated October 15, 2024 18:26\n\nThere are a few special Tonies that include pre-loaded content on them, but they can also function as Creative-Tonies! Currently, these special Tonies include the LeVar Burton Tonie, the GoNoodle x tonies® Mindfulness Tonie, the Calm Tonie, the Steiff Hoppie Rabbit and Jimmy Bear Tonies, the Sleepy Sheep and Sleepy Bear Night Light Tonies, and the limited edition Purple People Tonie (no longer available).\n\n \n\nHere's how to edit/delete content on your special Creative-Tonie:\n\nUsing the mytonies app\n\niframe\n\n  1. Open the mytonies app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Collection__9_.jpg\n\n  2. Tap on the 'Creative-Tonies' header.\nImage: CT_Header__7_.jpg\n\n  3. Tap the special Creative-Tonie you want to edit/delete content from.\nImage: CT_Jimmy__1_.jpg\n\n  4. Tap the 'Edit' button on the right-hand side of the screen. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew to tonies®: Top questions for first time listeners! – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036391406994-New-to-tonies-Top-questions-for-first-time-listeners)\nciteturn785search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Once your Toniebox 1 has synced with your Wi-Fi, and you've uploaded your Tonies, you can take it offline to play content.\n\n# New to tonies®: Top questions for first time listeners!\n\n#### Welcome to the tonies® family! 🎉  \n\nWe’re thrilled to have you join us and start building your collection. Here’s a quick guide to answer some of the most commonly asked questions by other Tonie-lovers:\n\nToniebox vs. Tonies: What’s the difference?\n\nToniebox 1 - Toniebox 1 is the audio player made for their hands, powered by their choices and designed to help them grow.\n\nToniebox 2 - Toniebox 2 is the next generation, the audio player designed for their hands, powered by their choices, and built to help them grow. Perfect for ages 1–12+, Toniebox 2 boosts independence and confidence as kids listen, play, and explore. Built to withstand years of bumps and tumbles, it gives them two ways to play. They can dive into favorite stories and songs with an ever-growing crew of Tonie characters.\n\nClassic Tonies - Collectible audio characters packed with their favorite songs and stories, designed for hands-on fun.\n\nCreative Tonie - Load up these audio characters with their favourite songs and stories. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us)\nciteturn785search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; [Button: Tonieboxes] [Button: Tonies] [Button: Tonieplay] [Button: Topics] [Button: Accessories] ... Toniebox 1 Toniebox 2 Toniebox Lite\n\n# How can we help?\n\n## Bluey is on the way!\n\nHave you got Bluey questions? Take a look at our FAQ and guides below.\n\nBluey Pre-Order Bluey FAQs\n\n# Browse by Product\n\n[Button: Tonieboxes] [Button: Tonies] [Button: Tonieplay] [Button: Topics] [Button: Accessories]\n\n## Categories\n\nToniebox 1 Toniebox 2 Toniebox Lite\n\nAll Tonies Classic Tonies Creative Tonies Pocket Tonies Book Tonies Night Lights My First Tonies Cuddle Tonies\n\nGetting Started Orders and Returns Account Mobile App and Website Audio Library All Other Articles Legal and Compliance\n\n## Browse by Topic\n\nFind help articles organized by common topics\n\nGetting Started Orders and Returns Account Mobile App and Website Audio Library\n\nSee all topics\n\n## Still can't find what you're looking for?\n\nSearch our Help Center for answers to your questions.\n\n[Input: Search for articles, guides, and help...]--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTonieboxes – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/categories/29036383531154-Tonieboxes)\nciteturn785search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; #### How do I set up a Toniebox 1?\n\n# Tonieboxes\n\nToniebox 1 Toniebox 2 Toniebox Lite\n\n## FAQs\n\n### Toniebox 1\n\nSetup\n\n#### How do I set up a Toniebox 1?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhy don’t we have Creative Tonies in the same colour as the new Toniebox 2's? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036582845970-Why-don-t-we-have-Creative-Tonies-in-the-same-colour-as-the-new-Toniebox-2-s)\nciteturn785search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # Why don’t we have Creative Tonies in the same colour as the new Toniebox 2's?\n\n# Why don’t we have Creative Tonies in the same colour as the new Toniebox 2's?\n\nWe don’t have Creative Tonies in the same colours as the new Toniebox 2, because we’ve introduced Rubie, our new brand character! Designed to inspire creativity for all kids, “Rubies amazing adventures” are full of fun ideas and imaginative ways to create your own stories, no matter which version of the Toniebox you have."
